*************************************************                 2637 1451
##### RESONANCE RANGE (adopted from JEFF-3.2)                     2637 1451
*************************************************                 2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
Reich-Moore resolved resonance parameters covering the energy     2637 1451
range 1.0e-5 eV to 350 keV were re-evaluated by M.C. Moxon [mox05]2637 1451
under a service agreement with the IAEA (2004).                   2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
Thermal cross sections                                            2637 1451
----------------------                                            2637 1451
Thermal cross section values are implicit in the resonance        2637 1451
parameters evaluated by M.C. Moxon [mox05]. The 2200 m/s cross    2637 1451
section values for T = 0 are as follows:                          2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
   Total               8.790 b                                    2637 1451
   Elastic scattering  7.476 b                                    2637 1451
   Radiative capture   1.314 b                                    2637 1451
                      (1.30  b  [mug03])                          2637 1451
                      (1.31  b  [mox02])                          2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
The expected 1/v dependence of the capture cross section below    2637 1451
the first positive resonance is accomplished by the addition of   2637 1451
several negative energy resonances. The radiation width of the    2637 1451
first bound level was adjusted so to reproduce the evaluated      2637 1451
thermal capture cross section.                                    2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
Resolved Resonance Region (up to 350 KeV)                         2637 1451
-----------------------------------------                         2637 1451
Resonance parameters up to 150 keV originate directly from the    2637 1451
measurements. Between 150 and 350 keV additional resonances for   2637 1451
l=2,3,4 were added so that they reproduce the observed average    2637 1451
capture cross sections. The detailed pointwise cross-section      2637 1451
shapes in this energy range may be incorrect.                     2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
The resonance integrals at T=300 K between 0.55 eV and 2 MeV are: 2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
   Total               115.5 b                                    2637 1451
   Elastic scattering  113.6 b                                    2637 1451
   Radiative capture   1.246 b                                    2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
Reich-Moore parameters were determined from the following         2637 1451
sources:                                                          2637 1451
                Capture analysis         Hockenbury+ [hoc69]      2637 1451
   7 - 325 keV  Capture & transmission   Hong+       [hon77]      2637 1451
   0 - 500 keV  Transmission analysis    Garg+       [gar78]      2637 1451
 2.5 - 200 keV  Capture analysis         Allen+      [all80]      2637 1451
  10 - 100 keV      "      "             Kaeppeler+  [kae83]      2637 1451
     ~ 359 eV   Capture analysis         Gayther+    [gay76]      2637 1451
 230 & 359 eV   Capture analysis         Borella+    [bor04]      2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
The parameters given in the report by Beer et al [bee78] appear   2637 1451
to be identical to those given in Hong et al's paper. The smooth  2637 1451
cross section in EXFOR is thought to be a calculation using       2637 1451
their fitted parameters.                                          2637 1451
  The EXFOR file lists the total cross section measurement by     2637 1451
Doil'nitsin et al [doi76], but the reference nor any other        2637 1451
details of the measurement could be obtained, so the data were    2637 1451
excluded from the analysis.                                       2637 1451
  Further detail on the adjustments and assumptions on the raw    2637 1451
experimental data can be found in the main reference [mox05].     2637 1451
                                                                  2637 1451
